    "The Motor and Liability XL treaty provides \"per event\" cover (\"every loss and/or occurrence and/or series of losses and/or occurrence any one event\"). However, there is also an annual aggregate limit of NGN 100mn increased from NGN60m for each layer.",
    "Majority of the Company\u2019s motor claims appear to be quickly settled on average within 23 days of lossdate. In view of the prevalence of motor liability claims in Nigeria, in large truck accident claims and possible aggravated court awards. It is recommended that transferring Motor risks to the Nigerian Insurance Liability pools would be more profitable strategy to spreading the risks. We note that the Nigerian Liability has been making profits for the recent past five years, guaranteed by reputable reinsurers with larger capacity than would be achieved from the excess of loss treaty."
